            <ArticleTitle>Late complication of aortocoronary venous bypass grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e9-e10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The problem of symptomatic, diffuse coronary artery disease not amenable to the established methods of medical or revascularizing therapies remains unsolved. Aortocoronary venous bypass grafting is a rare treatment modality bearing considerable risks. We report on a further complication of the method.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
